{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"polyfills","title":"Polyfills: Implement It Yourself","group":"Modern JS & Best Practices","order":62,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Re-implementing built-ins is the classic way interviewers test understanding of <code>this</code>, prototypes, closures and promises. Each implementation below is tested against the real thing.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-brackets\"></i>Array.prototype.map / filter / reduce</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>Array.prototype.myMap = function (callback, thisArg) {\n  if (typeof callback !== \"function\") throw new TypeError(callback + \" is not a function\");\n  const result = new Array(this.length);\n  for (let i = 0; i &lt; this.length; i++) {\n    if (i in this) result[i] = callback.call(thisArg, this[i], i, this);   // skip holes\n  }\n  return result;\n};\nArray.prototype.myFilter = function (callback, thisArg) {\n  const result = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i &lt; this.length; i++) {\n    if (i in this &amp;&amp; callback.call(thisArg, this[i], i, this)) result.push(this[i]);\n  }\n  return result;\n};\nArray.prototype.myReduce = function (callback, ...init) {\n  let i = 0, acc;\n  if (init.length) acc = init[0];\n  else {\n    while (i &lt; this.length &amp;&amp; !(i in this)) i++;\n    if (i &gt;= this.length) throw new TypeError(\"Reduce of empty array with no initial value\");\n    acc = this[i++];\n  }\n  for (; i &lt; this.length; i++) if (i in this) acc = callback(acc, this[i], i, this);\n  return acc;\n};\n\nconst nums = [1, 2, 3, 4];\nconsole.log(nums.myMap((n) =&gt; n * 2), nums.map((n) =&gt; n * 2));\nconsole.log(nums.myFilter((n) =&gt; n % 2), nums.myReduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b), nums.myReduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b, 10));\nconsole.log([1, , 3].myMap((x) =&gt; x), [1, , 3].map((x) =&gt; x));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 2, 4, 6, 8 ] [ 2, 4, 6, 8 ]\n[ 1, 3 ] 10 20\n[ 1, &lt;1 empty item&gt;, 3 ] [ 1, &lt;1 empty item&gt;, 3 ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-link\"></i>Function.prototype.bind / call</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>Function.prototype.myCall = function (context, ...args) {\n  context = context ?? globalThis;\n  const key = Symbol(\"fn\");                 // unique key: no clash with existing props\n  context[key] = this;\n  try {\n    return context[key](...args);           // implicit binding does the work\n  } finally {\n    delete context[key];\n  }\n};\nFunction.prototype.myBind = function (context, ...preset) {\n  const fn = this;\n  function bound(...later) {\n    // when called with `new`, ignore the bound context\n    return new.target ? new fn(...preset, ...later) : fn.apply(context, [...preset, ...later]);\n  }\n  bound.prototype = Object.create(fn.prototype);\n  return bound;\n};\n\nfunction intro(greeting, mark) { return `${greeting}, ${this.name}${mark}`; }\nconst asha = { name: \"Asha\" };\nconsole.log(intro.myCall(asha, \"Hello\", \"!\"));\nconsole.log(intro.myBind(asha, \"Hi\")(\"?\"), Object.keys(asha));\n\nfunction Point(x, y) { this.x = x; this.y = y; }\nconst PointAtX1 = Point.myBind(null, 1);\nconst p = new PointAtX1(2);\nconsole.log(p.x, p.y, p instanceof Point);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Hello, Asha!\nHi, Asha? [ 'name' ]\n1 2 true</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-join-2\"></i>Promise.all and Promise.allSettled</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function promiseAll(iterable) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n    const items = [...iterable];\n    const results = new Array(items.length);\n    let remaining = items.length;\n    if (remaining === 0) return resolve(results);\n    items.forEach((item, i) =&gt; {\n      Promise.resolve(item).then((value) =&gt; {\n        results[i] = value;                 // keep INPUT order, not finish order\n        if (--remaining === 0) resolve(results);\n      }, reject);                           // first rejection wins\n    });\n  });\n}\nconst promiseAllSettled = (iterable) =&gt;\n  promiseAll([...iterable].map((p) =&gt;\n    Promise.resolve(p).then(\n      (value) =&gt; ({ status: \"fulfilled\", value }),\n      (reason) =&gt; ({ status: \"rejected\", reason })\n    )));\n\nconst delay = (ms, v) =&gt; new Promise((r) =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; r(v), ms));\nconsole.log(await promiseAll([delay(20, \"slow\"), delay(5, \"fast\"), 3]));\nconsole.log(await promiseAll([]));\nawait promiseAll([delay(5, 1), Promise.reject(new Error(\"fail\"))]).catch((e) =&gt; console.log(e.message));\nconsole.log(await promiseAllSettled([1, Promise.reject(\"no\")]));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 'slow', 'fast', 3 ]\n[]\nfail\n[\n  { status: 'fulfilled', value: 1 },\n  { status: 'rejected', reason: 'no' }\n]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-circle-dashed-check\"></i>Promise.race and a mini Promise</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const promiseRace = (iterable) =&gt;\n  new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n    for (const p of iterable) Promise.resolve(p).then(resolve, reject);\n  });\n\nclass MyPromise {\n  #state = \"pending\"; #value; #handlers = [];\n  constructor(executor) {\n    const settle = (state) =&gt; (value) =&gt; {\n      if (this.#state !== \"pending\") return;\n      if (state === \"fulfilled\" &amp;&amp; value &amp;&amp; typeof value.then === \"function\") {\n        return value.then(settle(\"fulfilled\"), settle(\"rejected\"));   // adopt thenables\n      }\n      this.#state = state; this.#value = value;\n      this.#handlers.forEach((h) =&gt; h());\n    };\n    try { executor(settle(\"fulfilled\"), settle(\"rejected\")); } catch (e) { settle(\"rejected\")(e); }\n  }\n  then(onFul, onRej) {\n    return new MyPromise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n      const run = () =&gt; queueMicrotask(() =&gt; {\n        const cb = this.#state === \"fulfilled\" ? onFul : onRej;\n        if (typeof cb !== \"function\") return (this.#state === \"fulfilled\" ? resolve : reject)(this.#value);\n        try { resolve(cb(this.#value)); } catch (e) { reject(e); }\n      });\n      this.#state === \"pending\" ? this.#handlers.push(run) : run();\n    });\n  }\n  catch(onRej) { return this.then(undefined, onRej); }\n}\n\nconsole.log(await promiseRace([new Promise((r) =&gt; setTimeout(r, 20, \"slow\")), \"instant\"]));\nnew MyPromise((res) =&gt; setTimeout(res, 5, 2))\n  .then((v) =&gt; v * 10)\n  .then((v) =&gt; { throw new Error(`boom at ${v}`); })\n  .catch((e) =&gt; e.message)\n  .then((msg) =&gt; console.log(\"MyPromise chain:\", msg));\nconst value = await new MyPromise((res) =&gt; res(new MyPromise((r) =&gt; r(\"adopted\"))));\nconsole.log(value);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>instant\nadopted\nMyPromise chain: boom at 20</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-copy\"></i>Deep clone, deep equal, flatten</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function deepClone(value, seen = new WeakMap()) {\n  if (value === null || typeof value !== \"object\") return value;\n  if (value instanceof Date) return new Date(value);\n  if (value instanceof RegExp) return new RegExp(value.source, value.flags);\n  if (seen.has(value)) return seen.get(value);            // handle cycles\n  if (value instanceof Map) {\n    const m = new Map(); seen.set(value, m);\n    value.forEach((v, k) =&gt; m.set(deepClone(k, seen), deepClone(v, seen)));\n    return m;\n  }\n  const copy = Array.isArray(value) ? [] : Object.create(Object.getPrototypeOf(value));\n  seen.set(value, copy);\n  for (const key of Reflect.ownKeys(value)) copy[key] = deepClone(value[key], seen);\n  return copy;\n}\nfunction deepEqual(a, b) {\n  if (Object.is(a, b)) return true;\n  if (typeof a !== \"object\" || typeof b !== \"object\" || !a || !b) return false;\n  if (Object.getPrototypeOf(a) !== Object.getPrototypeOf(b)) return false;\n  const ka = Reflect.ownKeys(a), kb = Reflect.ownKeys(b);\n  return ka.length === kb.length &amp;&amp; ka.every((k) =&gt; deepEqual(a[k], b[k]));\n}\nconst flatten = (arr, depth = Infinity) =&gt;\n  depth &lt; 1 ? arr.slice() : arr.reduce((acc, x) =&gt; acc.concat(Array.isArray(x) ? flatten(x, depth - 1) : [x]), []);\n\nconst src = { d: new Date(0), list: [1, { two: 2 }], map: new Map([[\"k\", [1]]]) };\nsrc.self = src;\nconst copy = deepClone(src);\nconsole.log(copy.self === copy, copy.list[1] !== src.list[1], copy.map.get(\"k\"));\nconsole.log(deepEqual({ a: [1, { b: 2 }] }, { a: [1, { b: 2 }] }), deepEqual([1], { 0: 1 }));\nconsole.log(flatten([1, [2, [3, [4]]]]), flatten([1, [2, [3]]], 1));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true true [ 1 ]\ntrue false\n[ 1, 2, 3, 4 ] [ 1, 2, [ 3 ] ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-broadcast\"></i>A tiny EventEmitter</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Emitter {\n  #events = new Map();\n  on(name, fn) {\n    (this.#events.get(name) ?? this.#events.set(name, []).get(name)).push(fn);\n    return () =&gt; this.off(name, fn);        // return an unsubscribe function\n  }\n  off(name, fn) {\n    this.#events.set(name, (this.#events.get(name) ?? []).filter((f) =&gt; f !== fn &amp;&amp; f.original !== fn));\n  }\n  once(name, fn) {\n    const wrapper = (...args) =&gt; { this.off(name, wrapper); fn(...args); };\n    wrapper.original = fn;\n    return this.on(name, wrapper);\n  }\n  emit(name, ...args) {\n    const list = [...(this.#events.get(name) ?? [])];   // copy: listeners may unsubscribe\n    list.forEach((fn) =&gt; fn(...args));\n    return list.length &gt; 0;\n  }\n}\nconst e = new Emitter();\nconst unsubscribe = e.on(\"msg\", (m) =&gt; console.log(\"A got\", m));\ne.once(\"msg\", (m) =&gt; console.log(\"B (once) got\", m));\ne.emit(\"msg\", 1);\ne.emit(\"msg\", 2);\nunsubscribe();\nconsole.log(e.emit(\"msg\", 3));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>A got 1\nB (once) got 1\nA got 2\nfalse</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Real polyfills check <code>if (!Array.prototype.x)</code> before defining, use <code>Object.defineProperty</code> to stay non-enumerable, and follow the spec's edge cases. In production, use core-js rather than hand-written versions.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why does a correct Promise.all polyfill need a counter instead of checking results.length?</summary><div><p>Results are written by index as promises settle in any order; assigning <code>results[2]</code> first makes <code>length</code> 3 immediately. A countdown of pending items is the reliable completion signal.</p></div></details></section>"}